# Atlas Journey — Protected Core Interaction

The Atlas concept journey (Body → Feedback → Adaptation → Participation, and the same pattern for other questions) is a **protected core interaction**.

## Must not change without explicit user approval

- Journey renderer (`JourneyView` / bond destination click targets)
- Concept click targets and bond `onFollow` wiring
- Journey state transitions (`followBond`, notice → settle, trail updates)
- Authored bond order / canonical relations used for progression
- Moving the next concept into decorative SVG or non-interactive chrome
- Invisible overlays above click targets
- Replacing working navigation to make the journey “feel more spatial”

## Allowed without rewriting the journey

- Subtle background structure
- Passive path traces
- Atmospheric responses
- Visualizing completed paths elsewhere (e.g. Living Thread, Atlas threshold)

Visual behavior wraps the interaction. It does not rewrite it.

## body-react special case

Do not introduce a separate journey renderer for `body-react` (or any single question) unless the user explicitly requests a new experiment and accepts that the protected click path must remain intact.
